Z||000000||montage||03-06-2001||12:10 PM||||I need to replace the rear swaybar end links on my 88 formula and would like to use polyurethane. My local auto parts store can only get the front. Are there any sources other than the Fiero Store? Also has anyone tried or have comments on the adjustable polyurethane end link kits sold by JC Whitney? If these work I would like to put them on both the front and rear. Thanks in advance.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ironhedno3||03-06-2001||06:31 PM||||either talk to ed parks at the fiero factory or call prothane and talk to bruce||||reg||6
Z||000002||gixxer||03-06-2001||06:42 PM||||The Fiero Store has 'em for $16.95.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||03-06-2001||11:57 PM||||Polyurethane endlinks are nothing but the same hardware as rubber end links used with poly bushings. Get two sets of front poly bushings and use one on the back. You just <I>might</I> have to use longer bolts, but you can get those for $0.10 apiece at toyur local hardware store.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||03-07-2001||11:45 AM||||Here at West Coast Fiero, we can supply you with solid sway bar end links. These are made from top quality Rockwell steel and high grade Hiem joints. They are more responsive than ployurathane, and have a much greater life span<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
